-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for Sphere3Axiom and SourceS3
-- (doc/br-universal.pdf, Axiom S3, Lemma ev3, Lemma loopeq3, Definition and
-- Proposition sigma3, Lemma s3paths, Corollary qS, Definition s, Proposition right,
-- Theorem main, Corollary transfer): one entry per declaration, generated from --opened and checked
-- against the note by kind.  Kinds:
--   types and levels: PtMap -> PtSec, PtEquiv, Maps.PMO, Equiv, isEquiv, isContr,
--     isProp, isConn, isTrunc, O2, O3, Over.Unloop, the numerals two / three / five
--     (K(Z,3) is spelled KK.K three here and KK.K (suc two) in H4Bilinear.Lev: the
--     conversion is made once, in SourceS3.e2), NatArith.plus (levels of cor11), KZ2,
--     kz2, KK.K, Integers.intAb (g-def, as MapFib.SourceS.g-def);
--   step 2 (s3-paths .. rep-pteq): HC -> STr.C -> Quot.Q -> Quot.image; Triple3.F / f0
--     and LiftG.Ex / Un / qs (LiftG is stated with Fb.Fib); the numeral four (levels of
--     K(B,5)); in Final.s and Final.s-eq the one boundary conversion Triple3[Z, Z/2,
--     Fhat].F = DeloopR.BR (numerals three / five against suc two / suc four, Fibres.Fib
--     / fpt, DeloopR.BR / br0) and qs = - ; [fpr] = - ; [SourceBR.p] (Fibres.fpr,
--     SourceBR.p); SourceBR.PStar.pstar (right);
--   by-definition steps of the text: ap3, ev3, loop2, loop3, evPt, ptcomp, subst,
--     ContractP.Tot / g / h, Equivalences.compose (comp2/3/4-def: one level per step),
--     the local f1, f2, sigma3, e2i, N1, N2, Psi3, e-*, comp*, c3, CupSquare.e1inv,
--     Circle.pointed-equiv;
--   loop-refl: the pointing parts of loop (f, refl) and (ap f, refl) agree by
--     computation (Maps.loop, D, Kf, idJR, kf-ap, loop-ap, trans, sym, trans-sym-l);
--   extras, not steps of the text (library-side, as SphereAxiom.Sphere.Refl.eq and
--     evPt-nat in pi3.opens and MapFib.SourceS.Sig.sigma-nat in mapfib.opens): Maps.D /
--     Kf / loop, Paths.idJR, Prelude.trans in Sphere3.Refl.eq, Sig3.comp3-def and
--     Sig3.sigma3-nat.  Bisected (28 Oct 2026): the checker reduces the .1 of a looping
--     applied to an argument (Maps.loop -> D) before comparing by arguments, even
--     between a point and its one-step unfolding ((loop3 G).1 c3 against
--     (loop2 (loop G)).1 ((loop2 e2i).1 x1): 0 by arguments); and Maps[.., f1 (refl
--     base)].loop against Maps[.., refl (f base)].loop unfolds loop instead of comparing
--     the module parameters.  Documented, not fixed.
